module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChowLemma.CoproductQuasiCompactMorphism
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChowLemma.CoproductSeparated
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ChowLemma.CoproductZariskiCover
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.CoproductFiniteType
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Morphisms.FinitePresentation
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.QuasiCompactFpqcLocalAtTarget
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.QuasiCompactZariskiLocalTarget
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.SeparatedVariants

/-!
# Finite presentation of a morphism out of a coproduct of algebraic spaces

Let a sheaf `P` on the big fppf site over `S` be the coproduct of a family of algebraic spaces
over `S` with legs `ι i`, and let `f : P ⟶ Y` be a morphism to an algebraic space over `S`.
Stacks 03XP part (3) reads finite presentation of `f` as three conditions, and each is settled
separately for such an `f`.

Local finite presentation needs nothing of the index type: it is Zariski local on the source,
and the ranges of the legs are a Zariski covering of `P`.  Quasi-separatedness needs nothing
either, because such an `f` is separated as soon as its restrictions are.

Quasi-compactness is the one condition which does **not** follow from quasi-compactness of the
restrictions: an infinite coproduct of quasi-compact morphisms need not be quasi-compact.  What
is enough is that over every affine test object of the site all but finitely many base changes
of the summands are empty, and that is how
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasiCompact_of_isColimit_cofan_of_cofinitely_isEmpty` is stated.
For a finite index type the hypothesis is vacuous and the statement is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasiCompact_of_isColimit_cofan`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_of_isZariskiCover`: local finite
  presentation is Zariski local on the source.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyOfFinitePresentation_of_isColimit_cofan`: a morphism out of
  a coproduct is locally of finite presentation as soon as its restrictions are.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isEmpty_points_pullback_of_preimage_range_eq_empty`: a fibre product
  has no points when the point set of one factor misses the preimage of the point set of the
  other.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasiCompact_of_isColimit_cofan_of_cofinitely_isEmpty`: a morphism
  out of a coproduct is quasi-compact when its restrictions are and all but finitely many of
  their base changes to an affine test object of the site are empty.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isSeparated_of_isColimit_cofan_small` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasiSeparated_of_isColimit_cofan`: the separatedness statement at
  a `u`-small index type, and the quasi-separatedness it gives.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isFinitePresentation_of_isColimit_cofan_of_cofinitely_isEmpty`: the
  three clauses together.

## Implementation notes

Local finite presentation is read off the pointwise criterion
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFinitePresentationAt` exactly as local finite type is read off
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFiniteTypeAt` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/CoproductFiniteType.lean`; the equivalence with the
pointwise criterion is conditions (1) and (2) of Stacks 0410.

The hypothesis of the quasi-compactness statement is phrased on the base changes
`pullback g (ι i ≫ f)` rather than on the summands themselves, because emptiness over the test
object is what the argument uses and what the Fitting stratification supplies: over an affine
test object a module of finite type is generated by finitely many sections, so only finitely
many Fitting rank strata meet it.  The finitely many surviving base changes are
jointly surjective on the points of the whole base change, since the legs of a coproduct cofan
are a Zariski covering (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isZariskiCover_range_cofan_inj`) and the
others have no points at all; a finite jointly point-surjective family of quasi-compact spaces
has quasi-compact target by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasiCompactSpace_of_finite_jointly_surjective'`.

That a base change of the coproduct is the coproduct of the base changes is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isColimitCofanMkPullback`, the universality of coproducts of fppf
sheaves; it is the same input as in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ChowLemma/CoproductQuasiCompactMorphism.lean`.

Three of the four statements are proved for an index type in an arbitrary universe which is
`u`-small, since that is the generality in which countable coproducts of algebraic spaces are
available, and `ℕ` is not of type `Type u`.  The separatedness statement
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isSeparated_of_isColimit_cofan` is proved in the source file only for
an index type in `Type u`, so it is transported here along
`CategoryTheory.Limits.Cofan.isColimitEquivOfEquiv`.

